ources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e911fa1a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 927, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:53\", \"token_count\": 288, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-21\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-21\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-21\\n\\n**Title**: Release v1.0 Gates\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-07-08\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-07-08**: Evan - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Task opened to track the release gates for the v1.0 milestone.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 21 sourc id src cu ciph 21 task id ciph 21 titl releas v1 0 gate status activ assigne evan prioriti normal date creat 2026 07 08 activ histori 2026 07 08 evan task creat open task open to track the releas gate for the v1 0 mileston\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e97842848a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-21-Release-v1-Gates.md\", \"id\": \"fc6c9f27fa56f965\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2704939820710556, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08547158867293658, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7022129, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-21-Release-v1-Gates.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e97842848a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-21-Release-v1-Gates.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-21-Release-v1-Gates.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1139, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:27\", \"token_count\": 635, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## Sign-off Basis\\n\\nSecurity sign-off on the AES-256 at-rest pipeline was withheld until the fail-closed deletion behavior for interrupted redaction runs (T015) was confirmed Completed — an unencrypted partial output left on disk after a crash would have undermined the encryption guarantee entirely. With that dependency cleared, the sign-off proceeded against the pipeline as implemented.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## What Was Reviewed\\n\\n- AES-256-GCM authenticated encryption applied to every redacted output file before it is written to its final location.\\n\\n- Key handling confined to process memory; no plaintext key material written to disk or logs.\\n\\n- Confirmed the pipeline degrades safely (refuses to write plaintext) if key material is unavailable, consistent with the fail-closed contract from T015.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## Follow-up Noted at Sign-off\\n\\nOn machines without a hardware TPM, the volume key is still derived from a user passphrase via PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 at 100k iterations. This is not a blocker for the AES-256 pipeline sign-off itself, but Diana flagged it as a hardening follow-up: moving to Argon2id would meaningfully raise the cost of offline brute-force against weak passphrases on non-TPM hardware.\\n\\n*Status*: AES-256 at-rest pipeline signed off as Completed. Passphrase-derived key hardening (Argon2id) tracked separately as a pre-v1.0 hardening item, not a sign-off condition.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 sign off basi secur sign off on the ae 256 at rest pipelin wa withheld until the fail close delet behavior for interrupt redact run t015 wa confirm complet an unencrypt partial output left on disk after a crash would have undermin the encrypt guarante entir with that depend clear the sign off proceed against the pipelin a implement sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 what wa review ae 256 gcm authent encrypt appli to everi redact output file befor it is written to it final locat key handl confin to process memori no plaintext key materi written to disk or log confirm the pipelin degrad safe refus to write plaintext if key materi is unavail consist with the fail close contract from t015 sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 follow up note at sign off on machin without a hardwar tpm the volum key is still deriv from a user passphras via pbkdf2 hmac sha256 at 100k iter this is not a blocker for the ae 256 pipelin sign off itself but diana flag it a a harden follow up move to argon2id would meaning rais the cost of offlin brute forc against weak passphras on non tpm hardwar status ae 256 at rest pipelin sign off a complet passphras deriv key harden argon2id track separ a a pre v1 0 harden item not a sign off condit\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e99eb05e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"id\": \"3d30fbd4bb571642\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2695661418926164, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09292513127516636, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6817285, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e99eb05e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1518, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:57\", \"token_count\": 466, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Background: Path Fix Cleared Packaging\\n\\nBackslash path-handling defects that previously broke Windows builds were fixed on 2026-08-10, and a Windows build artifact was successfully produced by 2026-08-12. Packaging itself is no longer the blocker.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Current Blocker: Missing Code-Signing Certificate\\n\\nThe produced build artifact is unsigned, which triggers a SmartScreen warning and Defender flagging the binary as untrusted.\\n\\n- **Impact**: Site IT policies commonly block execution of unsigned/SmartScreen-flagged binaries outright, which would prevent installation on target deployment workstations without a manual security-policy override.\\n\\n- **Root Cause**: No code-signing certificate has been procured or configured in the Windows build pipeline yet.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Path to Resolution\\n\\nProcuring a code-signing certificate and wiring signing into the release build step is the only remaining item before this clears the T029 Windows compatibility gate — and, by extension, the T011 release checklist, which is holding on this exact signing gap alongside the T005 image slim-down.\\n\\n*Audit Status*: Active. Build produces successfully; signing certificate procurement is the sole open blocker.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 background path fix clear packag backslash path handl defect that previous broke window build were fix on 2026 08 10 and a window build artifact wa success produc by 2026 08 12 packag itself is no longer the blocker sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 current blocker miss code sign certif the produc build artifact is unsign which trigger a smartscreen warn and defend flag the binari a untrust impact site it polici common block execut of unsign smartscreen flag binari outright which would prevent instal on target deploy workstat without a manual secur polici overrid root caus no code sign certif ha been procur or configur in the window build pipelin yet sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 path to resolut procur a code sign certif and wire sign into the releas build step is the onli remain item befor this clear the t029 window compat gate and by extens the t011 releas checklist which is hold on this exact sign gap alongsid the t005 imag slim down audit status activ build produc success sign certif procur is the sole open blocker\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9aa652a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"id\": \"7d9dbdfb5b6d7c2f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2632022185352393, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.05669645505034182, \"vector_similarity\": 0.745049, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9aa652a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1340, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:48\", \"token_count\": 387, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-05\\n\\n<table>\\n<thead>\\n<tr>\\n<th style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Task</th>\\n<th style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Item</th>\\n<th style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Status</th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody>\\n<tr>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">T001</td>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Core Redaction Engine</td>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Completed (2026-06-05)</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">T002</td>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Financial Regex Detection</td>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Completed (2026-06-08)</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td sty