unication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1495, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:06\", \"token_count\": 424, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-36\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Windows Path Handling\\n\\n**Channel**: #releases\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 10:19] Evan**: Windows builds have been failing on path separators — the ingestion logic has backslash assumptions baked in that don't hold up on Windows.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 10:34] Bob**: Quick search-and-replace for the separator, or something more thorough?\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 10:39] Evan**: More thorough — moving the path handling to be OS-aware instead of hardcoded, so this doesn't come back the next time we touch it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 10:41] Bob**: LGTM.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 12:46] Charlie**: What about the temp directory? I remember some older code assuming a Linux-style path there too.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 13:00] Evan**: Already on it. Fixing that in the same pass so it respects the OS-level temp location instead of guessing.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 13:01] Alice**: How's this looking for a first test build?\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 13:03] Evan**: Once the path fix holds up under test, I should be able to produce a build artifact from it.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 36 slack thread window path handl channel releas date 2026 08 10 2026 08 1010 19 evan window build have been fail on path separ the ingest logic ha backslash assumpt bake in that don t hold up on window 2026 08 1010 34 bob quick search and replac for the separ or someth more thorough 2026 08 1010 39 evan more thorough move the path handl to be o awar instead of hardcod so this doesn t come back the next time we touch it 2026 08 1010 41 bob lgtm 2026 08 10 12 46 charli what about the temp directori i rememb some older code assum a linux style path there too 2026 08 10 13 00 evan alreadi on it fix that in the same pas so it respect the o level temp locat instead of guess 2026 08 10 13 01 alic how s this look for a first test build 2026 08 10 13 03 evan onc the path fix hold up under test i should be abl to produc a build artifact from it\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8fd13168a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-10-windows-path-handling.md\", \"id\": \"861669a2b04e3fa7\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2672443605294131, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10121500075630442, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6546462, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-10-windows-path-handling.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8fd13168a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-10-windows-path-handling.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-10-windows-path-handling.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1051, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:11\", \"token_count\": 322, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-37\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Windows Signing Gap\\n\\n**Channel**: #releases\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 09:14] Evan**: Windows Defender and SmartScreen are both flagging the build for pilot testers — unsigned binaries get treated as untrusted by default.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:13] Alice**: Is the missing code-signing certificate the actual blocker here?\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:14] Evan**: Yes. We still don't have one. Until we do, every pilot install is going to trip a warning at best, get blocked outright at worst.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:16] Diana**: Release blocker?\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:17] Bob**: Copy.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:18] Evan**: It stays open as far as I'm concerned — this isn't something we can work around on the engineering side, we need the certificate.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:59] Alice**: Let's keep it open on the release gate rather than pushing it off the board. I'll chase the certificate process.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 37 slack thread window sign gap channel releas date 2026 09 02 2026 09 02 09 14 evan window defend and smartscreen are both flag the build for pilot tester unsign binari get treat a untrust by default 2026 09 02 10 13 alic is the miss code sign certif the actual blocker here 2026 09 02 10 14 evan yes we still don t have one until we do everi pilot instal is go to trip a warn at best get block outright at worst 2026 09 02 10 16 diana releas blocker 2026 09 02 10 17 bob copi 2026 09 02 1018 evan it stay open a far a i m concern this isn t someth we can work around on the engin side we need the certif 2026 09 02 10 59 alic let s keep it open on the releas gate rather than push it off the board i ll chase the certif process\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e911fa1a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"id\": \"4223f88ffbddf892\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.26613539283512366, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07506127547874811, \"vector_similarity\": 0.711975, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\