for simple cases, but it's completely breaking on documents with nested Form XObjects.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:43] Charlie**: Yeah, I looked into it. The underlying rendering library we're using (`pdf-lib-core`) has a known bug in how it handles coordinates for XObjects when a parent transform is applied.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:55] Alice**: Can we patch it?\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:56] Charlie**: No.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:35] Charlie**: It's deep in their C++ core. I've opened an issue with the upstream maintainers, but they haven't responded.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:37] Evan**: We can't wait for an upstream fix if we're hitting the release gate. Can we work around it by flattening the PDFs first?\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:51] Charlie**: Flattening might work but it'll blow up the file size and we might lose some text layers.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 12:29] Alice**: @Diana, @Charlie, let's leave high-DPI rendering blocked for now. We need to decide if we can ship with this limitation or if we need a different rendering library entirely.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 12:32] Diana**: Agreed. It only affects a small subset of complex documents, but we should document it as a known issue.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 58 slack thread high dpi upstream block channel cipherdoc date 2026 09 10 2026 09 1010 41 diana bad news on the high dpi render fix the rotat fix charli push work for simpl case but it s complet break on document with nest form xobject 2026 09 1010 43 charli yeah i look into it the under render librari we re use pdf lib core ha a known bug in how it handl coordin for xobject when a parent transform is appli 2026 09 1010 55 alic can we patch it 2026 09 1010 56 charli no 2026 09 10 11 35 charli it s deep in their c core i ve open an issu with the upstream maintain but they haven t respond 2026 09 10 11 37 evan we can t wait for an upstream fix if we re hit the releas gate can we work around it by flatten the pdfs first 2026 09 10 11 51 charli flatten might work but it ll blow up the file size and we might lose some text layer 2026 09 10 12 29 alic diana charli let s leav high dpi render block for now we need to decid if we can ship with this limit or if we need a differ render librari entir 2026 09 10 12 32 diana agre it onli affect a small subset of complex document but we should document it a a known issu\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9310f048a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"id\": \"72425f09d11fcc84\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28988057793240063, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12407425418914375, \"vector_similarity\": 0.676762, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9310f048a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1371, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:29\", \"token_count\": 414, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nDiana walked the high-latency handshake timeout. The team left handshake work blocked; no timeout-bump workaround. Path still depends on the encryption workstream.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Diana**: Handshake triage — nominal latency was fine; Bob's earlier validation held up on the local network. On a simulated high-latency link the handshake never finishes. It times out.\\n\\n**Bob**: That matches what I expected once we left the happy path. The prototype assumed round trips stay quick. High latency breaks the exchange.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Is this an encryption cost problem? AES-256 on the wire path is in the dependency chain here.\\n\\n**Bob**: It's related. The handshake still has to complete under that load, and on a slow link it doesn't. I don't have a fix that keeps the current exchange as-is.\\n\\n**Evan**: Bumping timeouts just hides it. If the link is slow enough, we still fail.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll leave the high-latency repro in place so we can re-check when encryption or the handshake design changes.\\n\\n**Alice**: Then we leave it. Handshake work stays blocked on timeouts under high latency. It depends on the encryption path, and we're not inventing a workaround in this meeting.\\n\\n**Bob**: Agreed — no timeout bump. We'll revisit when the crypto path moves.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari diana walk the high latenc handshak timeout the team left handshak work block no timeout bump workaround path still depend on the encrypt workstream sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript diana handshak triag nomin latenc wa fine bob s earlier valid held up on the local network on a simul high latenc link the handshak never finish it time out bob that match what i expect onc we left the happi path the prototyp assum round trip stay quick high latenc break the exchang charli is this an encrypt cost problem ae 256 on the wire path is in the depend chain here bob it s relat the handshak still ha to complet under that load and on a slow link it doesn t i don t have a fix that keep the current exchang ais evan bump timeout just hide it if the link is slow enough we still fail diana i ll leav the high latenc repro in place so we can re check when encrypt or the handshak design chang alic then we leav it handshak work stay block on timeout under high latenc it depend on the encrypt path and we re not invent a workaround in this meet bob agre no timeout bump we ll revisit when the crypto path move\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"id\": \"edcdc1df7188b1a3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2857838679324006, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12407425418914375, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6631063, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1463, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:18\", \"token_count\": 417, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-38\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Windows Build Artifact\\n\\n**Channel**: #releases\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:05] Evan**: Path fix unblocked the Windows packaging attempt — I've got a build artifact out the other end now.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:06] Bob**: Does it actually run, or just build?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:24] Evan**: Runs. Installed it on a Windows box and it's passing the same sanity checks we run on Linux.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:26] Diana**: Does this mean Windows compatibility is done?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:36] Evan**: The engineering work for the Windows build is complete — packaging works, the binary is sound. Code-signing is a separate item we haven't even started on yet, so I wouldn't call the whole thing closed.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:45] Alice**: Understood, we'll track signing on its own. Good progress on the build itself.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 38 slack thread window build artifact channel releas date 2026 08 12 2026 08 12 09 05 evan path fix unblock the window packag attempt i ve got a build artifact out the other end now 2026 08 12 09 06 bob doe it actual run or just build 2026 08 12 09 24 evan run instal it on a window box and it s pass the same saniti check we run on linux 2026 08 12 09 26 diana doe this mean window compat is done 2026 08 12 09 36 evan the engin work for the window build is complet packag work the binari is sound code sign is a separ item we haven t even start on yet so i wouldn t call the whole thing close 2026 08 12 09 45 alic understood we ll track sign on it own good progress on the build itself\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8e7f9688a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"id\": \"61bccaf0a0dfface\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28561677510302325, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11115879300431895, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6926854, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8e7f9688a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 859, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:30\", \"token_count\": 268, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-39\\n\\n# Slack Thread: License Audit\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-09\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 11:13] Diana**: Starting the third-party license audit across the dependency tree — need a full inventory before we sign off on anything for release.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 12:37] Alice**: Watch closely for GPL or AGPL. Our client agreements rule out shipping copyleft code in the core engine.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 12:46] Diana**: That's exactly what I'm scanning for, using license-checker against the dependency manifests to flag anything outside MIT/Apache/BSD.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 13:19] Bob**: Are you following transitive dependencies too? A clean top-level library can still pull in something restrictive underneath.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 13:24] Diana**: Yes, doing a recursive pass, not just the direct dependencies.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 13:51] Evan**: Want a hand with the Docker base image layers once the app-level scan is done?\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 14:07] Diana**: That'd help. Still working through the results — nothing conclusive to report yet, I'll have the full inventory soon.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 39 slack thread licens audit channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 09 2026 08 09 11 13 diana start the third parti licens audit across the depend tree need a full inventori befor we sign off on anyth for releas 2026 08 09 12 37 alic watch close for gpl or agpl our client agreement rule out ship copyleft code in the core engin 2026 08 09 12 46 diana that s exact what i m scan for use licens checker against the depend manifest to flag anyth outsid mit apach bsd 2026 08 09 13 19 bob are you follow transit depend too a clean top level librari can still pull in someth restrict underneath 2026 08 09 13 24 diana yes do a recurs pas not just the direct depend 2026 08 09 13 51 evan want a hand with the docker base imag layer onc the app level scan is done 2026 08 09 14 07 diana that d help still work through the result noth conclus to report yet i ll have the full inventori soon\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e90df4e28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-license-audit.md\", \"id\": \"f45d87f25a79b4cd\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28532435010302326, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11115879300431895, \"vector_similarity\": 0.69171065, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-license-audit.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e90df4e28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-license-audit.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-license-audit.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1085, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:57\", \"token_count\": 310, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-10\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Pre-Release Audit\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nPre-release gate review: Docker slim/CVE, Windows signing, and upstream high-DPI remain open. Audit-log path still a hold — CLI schema and emitted records don't match.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-10\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Pre-Release Audit\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Alice**: We're in pre-release mode. Gate check first: Docker slim-down and CVE work is still open, Windows signing is still open, and we're still blocked upstream on the high-DPI rendering bug. Those stay on the board. Diana, where are we on the audit-log gate?\\n\\n**Diana**: Still a hold. The CLI path and the log records aren't matching the schema we defined. That undercuts the audit trail as release evidence.\\n\\n**Bob**: I've been wiring audit-log generation into the CLI. The shape coming out still isn't consistent with what the schema expects — I've got another pass queued.\\n\\n**Charlie**: So this isn't a packaging issue — it's schema versus emitted records?\\n\\n**Diana**: Yes. Until those match, I can't clear the audit gate.\\n\\n**Evan**: That stacks on top of the Docker and Windows holds Alice listed. Release isn't opening with any of those unresolved.\\n\\n**Alice**: Correct. Security-gate work stays open — Docker slim-down, Windows signing, and we keep the audit mismatch visible as a release blocker. No one closes those today.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll keep the audit-log gate red until schema and records match.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari pre releas gate review docker slim cve window sign and upstream high dpi remain open audit log path still a hold cli schema and emit record don t match sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript alic we re in pre releas mode gate check first docker slim down and cve work is still open window sign is still open and we re still block upstream on the high dpi render bug those stay on the board diana where are we on the audit log gate diana still a hold the cli path and the log record aren t match the schema we defin that undercut the audit trail a releas evid bob i ve been wire audit log generat into the cli the shape come out still isn t consist with what the schema expect i ve got anoth pas queu charli so this isn t a packag issu it s schema versus emit record diana yes until those match i can t clear the audit gate evan that stack on top of the docker and window hold alic list releas isn t open with ani of those unresolv alic correct secur gate work stay open docker slim down window sign and we keep the audit mismatch visibl a a releas blocker no one close those today diana i ll keep the audit log gate red until schema and record match\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e94edcc88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"id\": \"be17298264309b61\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2809018622736459, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09824333181949413, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7071051, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e94edcc88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1495, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:06\", \"token_count\": 424, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-05\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Performance Benchmarks Blocker\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-09\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nEvan opened with the bare-metal blocker: scripts are ready, but the dedicated node still isn't provisioned. The team rejected shared/virtualized boxes as publishable evidence.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-05\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Performance Benchmarks Blocker\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-09\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Evan**: Quick update on bare-metal benchmarks — scripts are ready and tested locally, but I still don't have the dedicated node provisioned. I've chased it twice this week already.\\n\\n**Bob**: Could we run against one of the shared dev boxes in the meantime, just to get a rough number?\\n\\n**Evan**: I'd rather not — those boxes are virtualized and shared with other teams, so any noisy-neighbor load would throw off the numbers we'd be publishing.\\n\\n**Diana**: Agreed. If we publish something based on a shared box, we can't stand behind it if someone challenges the release claims later.\\n\\n**Alice**: Keep chasing the real hardware then. Let's not publish anything until we have it.\\n\\n**Bob**: Fine by me. Shared-box numbers aren't worth the argument later.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 05 firefli transcript perform benchmark blocker date 2026 08 09 particip alic pm bob backend diana qa evan devop summari evan open with the bare metal blocker script are readi but the dedic node still isn t provis the team reject share virtual box a publish evid sourc id src me