nothing that touches the active redaction path.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 10:41] Diana**: What's next after the prototype?\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 11:47] Bob**: Need to check it holds up under real network delay, not just on my two test nodes on the same switch. That's the next pass.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 26 slack thread node sync handshak prototyp channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 06 2026 08 06 09 30 bob start on the replic handshak for the zero trust node sync first requir is that two node have to authent each other befor either one accept replic entri 2026 08 06 09 37 evan how s a node prove who it is right now 2026 08 06 09 38 bob each node ha a regist ident it present at connect time if the peer doesn t recogn it the connect get drop befor ani data move 2026 08 06 09 49 charli doe the handshak add notic overhead to the redact job run on the same box 2026 08 06 10 40 bob neglig so far it s a short exchang befor the sync session open noth that touch the activ redact path 2026 08 06 10 41 diana what s next after the prototyp 2026 08 06 11 47 bob need to check it hold up under real network delay not just on my two test node on the same switch that s the next pas\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8f020a28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"id\": \"6657f131b0d26923\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33204514590078393, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20401148700111993, \"vector_similarity\": 0.63079035, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8f020a28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1079, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:24\", \"token_count\": 317, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-33\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Offline Batch Run\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 08:58] Diana**: Harness is ready, so I'm running a full batch through it with the network blocked at the OS level. Kicking off now.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 11:28] Diana**: Batch is still running clean — no unexpected outbound connection attempts logged so far.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 09:30] Diana**: Batch finished offline. Signing off, but flagging one thing: there's a roughly 45-second hang at startup where something in the licence check reaches for a remote endpoint before it gives up and falls back to the local path.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 09:42] Bob**: 45 seconds is a long time to sit there. Is that the encryption-pipeline license check?\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 10:54] Diana**: Looks that way — depends on the encryption work, so I'm not touching that path here. Recording it and moving on.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 10:56] Alice**: So we're calling this signed off?\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 11:08] Diana**: I'll close this out, but I want to be clear this is a preliminary offline pass — not a compliance certification. The 45-second hang is noted, not resolved.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 33 slack thread offlin batch run channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 08 last activ 2026 08 10 2026 08 08 08 58 diana har is readi so i m run a full batch through it with the network block at the o level kick off now 2026 08 08 11 28 diana batch is still run clean no unexpect outbound connect attempt log so far 2026 08 10 09 30 diana batch finish offlin sign off but flag one thing there s a rough 45 second hang at startup where someth in the licenc check reach for a remot endpoint befor it give up and fall back to the local path 2026 08 10 09 42 bob 45 second is a long time to sit there is that the encrypt pipelin licens check 2026 08 1010 54 diana look that way depend on the encrypt work so i m not touch that path here record it and move on 2026 08 1010 56 alic so we re call this sign off 2026 08 10 11 08 diana i ll close this out but i want to be clear this is a preliminari offlin pas not a complianc certif the 45 second hang is note not resolv\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9238f288a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-offline-batch-run.md\", \"id\": \"c04a1f0066314f5d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3313000209007839, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20401148700111993, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6283066, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-offline-batch-run.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9238f288a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-offline-batch-run.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-offline-batch-run.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1193, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:41\", \"token_count\": 353, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-22\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Storage Quota Management Design\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 09:30] Evan**: Starting on storage quota management. We need to keep `cipherdoc` from filling up the disk on these workstations, especially on large batch jobs.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 09:39] Evan**: Implementing a disk-usage monitor loop. It'll check available space before starting any new redaction job.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 09:41] Alice**: What's the threshold?\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:08] Evan**: Going with a hard 500MB floor for now. If free space drops below that, the engine pauses and alerts the user.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:26] Diana**: We also need a way to clear the cache — the `/tmp` folder doesn't always clean up properly after a crash.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:41] Evan**: I'll add a purge-cache option and run a sweep on startup too.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:44] Evan**: @Bob, can we get a hook in the `FileStreamer` to report current disk usage for the active job?\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 11:30] Bob**: Sure, I'll add a `get_quota_usage()` method to the stream controller.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 22 slack thread storag quota manag design channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 04 2026 08 04 09 30 evan start on storag quota manag we need to keep cipherdoc from fill up the disk on these workstat especi on larg batch job 2026 08 04 09 39 evan implement a disk usag monitor loop it ll check avail space befor start ani new redact job 2026 08 04 09 41 alic what s the threshold 2026 08 04 10 08 evan go with a hard 500mb floor for now if free space drop below that the engin paus and alert the user 2026 08 04 10 26 diana we also need a way to clear the cach the tmp folder doesn t alway clean up proper after a crash 2026 08 04 10 41 evan i ll add a purg cach option and run a sweep on startup too 2026 08 04 10 44 evan bob can we get a hook in the filestream to report current disk usag for the activ job 2026 08 04 11 30 bob sure i ll add a get _ quota _ usag method to the stream control\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8e0ea928a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-storage-quota-monitor.md\", \"id\": \"9a05aa4017f04966\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32641168590078395, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20401148700111993, \"vector_similarity\": 0.61201215, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-storage-quota-monitor.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8e0ea928a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-storage-quota-monitor.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-storage-quota-monitor.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1088, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:37\", \"token_count\": 344, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-08\\n\\n# Slack Thread: API Authentication Deferral\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-28\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-20\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 13:07] Bob**: Looking into REST API auth for v1.0. Do we need a full auth story now, or is trusted local network enough for the first release?\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 13:22] Diana**: Given the PII involved, something robust would be nice. But if this is strictly local-network-only, we might not need it for v1.0.\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 14:00] Bob**: Doing a short study either way — what we'd need if we keep auth in scope versus what we defer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-29 14:23] Diana**: If we defer, we should at least write down the v1.1 requirements so we don't lose them.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:01] Alice**: Team, we're falling behind on core engine work. I'm deferring the auth module to v1.1. For v1.0, the API assumes a trusted local network.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:19] Diana**: Manageable if we stay local-network-only. I'll note the deferral.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:21] Bob**: Fine. I'll keep the seams clean so adding auth later isn't a rewrite.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 11:04] Bob**: Still deferred — capturing v1.1 auth requirements while we remember them: REST auth with rotation support, since v1.0 is local-network-only.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 11:06] Diana**: Agreed. Folding that into the deferred-work notes so it survives until v1.1 planning.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 10:11] Alice**: Rechecked release scope for v1.0 — auth stays deferred to post-v1.0.0. Trusted-network assumption still holds.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 08 slack thread api authent deferr channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 28 last activ 2026 08 20 2026 06 28 13 07 bob look into rest api auth for v1 0 do we need a full auth stori now or is trust local network enough for the first releas 2026 06 28 13 22 diana given the pii involv someth robust would be nice but if this is strict local network onli we might not need it for v1 0 2026 06 28 14 00 bob do a short studi either way what we d need if we keep auth in scope versus what we defer 2026 06 29 14 23 diana if we defer we should at least write down the v1 1 requir so we don t lose them 2026 06 30 09 01 alic team we re fall behind on core engin work i m defer the auth modul to v1 1 for v1 0 the api assum a trust local network 2026 06 30 09 19 diana manag if we stay local network onli i ll note the deferr 2026 06 30 09 21 bob fine i ll keep the seam clean so ad auth later isn t a rewrit 2026 08 0511 04 bob still defer captur v1 1 auth requir while we rememb them rest auth with rotat support sinc v1 0 is local network onli 2026 08 0511 06 diana agre fold that into the defer work note so it surviv until v1 1 plan 2026 08 20 10 11 alic recheck releas scope for v1 0 auth stay defer to post v1 0 0 trust network assumpt still hold\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197