l completion, and the temp files are gone after each. No leftovers.\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 09:30] Charlie**: Good. Secure deletion confirmed — I'll close this out.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 29 slack thread ocr temp cleanup hook channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 09 last activ 2026 08 11 2026 08 09 09 21 charli cleanup hook are in cover both the failur path and the normal complet path use the site inventori from the trace so noth s left out 2026 08 09 09 36 bob what happen if the process get kill outright instead of fail clean 2026 08 09 09 39 charli can t hook a hard kill direct but between the failur hook and the complet hook we cover everyth the ocr branch can reach on it own 2026 08 09 10 49 diana i ll run it against the qa scenario that left orphan file last week and see if it actual clear them 2026 08 11 09 09 diana confirm ran it through both the failur case and a normal complet and the temp file are gone after each no leftov 2026 08 11 09 30 charli good secur delet confirm i ll close this out\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8cf58228a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-ocr-temp-cleanup-hooks.md\", \"id\": \"2b3aacf13c8e9311\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3013803128571063, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.16320918979586613, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6237796, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-ocr-temp-cleanup-hooks.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8cf58228a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-ocr-temp-cleanup-hooks.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-ocr-temp-cleanup-hooks.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1012, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:51\", \"token_count\": 297, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-06\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Docker Image Size Optimization\\n\\n**Channel**: #releases\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-25\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-25 09:35] Diana**: @Evan, I just pulled the latest `cipherdoc` image. It's 2.1GB! That's way too big for a local runtime deployment. Reopening the Docker packaging task.\\n\\n**[2026-08-01 09:30] Evan**: Whoa, 2.1GB, and we still haven't closed out the CVE verification either. Looks like the full Ubuntu base is a big part of the bloat. I'll put together a multi-stage build plan targeting somewhere around 450MB.\\n\\n**[2026-08-01 09:33] Diana**: That'd get it onto standard dev laptops without eating all the disk space. Let's aim for that.\\n\\n**[2026-08-01 10:04] Evan**: Multi-stage build plan is in place. Stripping out the build-time dependencies from the final artifact.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 13:11] Evan**: The multi-stage split alone still leaves the base layer too large. Swapping from `ubuntu:22.04` to `alpine:latest` as the base. Had some issues with `glibc` vs `musl`, but `gcompat` seems to fix it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 15:21] Evan**: Alpine swap didn't get us all the way there either. Just removed the unused OCR and runtime packages we aren't shipping in this build.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:00] Diana**: Checked the size and ran the CVE scan. We're still over the ~450MB target, and the CVE verification is still failing.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:10] Evan**: Yeah, not where we need to be yet. There's still fluff in the Python site-packages layer, and I need to chase down what's tripping the CVE scan.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:13] Diana**: Reopened status stands until both the size and the CVE check are clean. I'll keep tracking it against the release checkl